      en: "The Teslim Balogun Stadium is a massive, highly active multi-purpose sporting arena located in Surulere, Lagos. Situated directly adjacent to the older National Stadium, it was completed in 2007 and named in honor of Teslim 'Thunder' Balogun, a legendary Nigerian footballer. With a seating capacity of over 24,000, the stadium is the beating heart of local Lagos sports, serving as the home ground for prominent football clubs like First Bank FC. Beyond football, the complex is heavily utilized for athletics, boxing, and massive political and religious gatherings, making it an indispensable part of the intense, daily social fabric of Lagos. Geography K7 — urban sports infrastructure and local football."
